This AI/ML module is responsible for risk prediction in the NER‑SmartRoute prototype. It uses cleaned datasets prepared by Member 6 (rainfall, elevation, slope, landslide history, and district mapping) to train a machine learning model (risk_model.pkl). The model takes four key inputs — rainfall, elevation, slope, and landslides — and outputs a risk level (LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH). Predictions for each district are stored in district_risk_predictions.csv for integration with GIS routing. The trained model is loaded in the backend (main.py) through the /predict_risk API, which allows both real‑time risk assessment and “what‑if” simulations. This module ensures that route recommendations and accessibility checks are informed by data‑driven risk analysis.
  
